 `results/` holds the published runs: the raw JSONL of each tool, with a note on what was compared.
 
+## Text in the charts
+
+The charts show text `report.py` did not write itself: a build's name and `--label`'s text from the command line, a panel's
+name from a results file (`pauses.jsonl`'s `step`), a version from `environment.txt`. Each of those is escaped as it is written
+into the SVG, once, in one place (`svg_text` for text between tags, `svg_attr` for an attribute value such as `aria-label`), so
+a label cannot close a text element, end an attribute or open a script, and every document is well-formed XML. The five XML
+characters (`&`, `<`, `>` and, in an attribute, `"` and `'`) are the only ones replaced: ordinary text is unchanged byte for
+byte, and a value that already looks escaped is shown as the text it is, not escaped twice. Characters XML 1.0 forbids even
+escaped (the C0 controls but tab, newline and carriage return, and the surrogates) are removed, since one would make the file
+unparseable; every other Unicode character (accents, CJK, emoji) is kept. The Markdown tables printed to stdout are a separate
+surface, not SVG markup, and are unchanged.
+
+`tests/bench/report-svg.py` guards this: ordinary, Unicode, entity, attribute-breakout and element-injection cases, each SVG
+parsed with `xml.etree.ElementTree`, plus a run of `report.py` itself with hostile `--builds` and `--label` values. Run it with
+`tests/bench/run.sh` (standard library only).
+
 Requires Python 3.9+; `tmux_check.py` also needs tmux. Pin runs to idle cores with `--cpus` for stable figures. See
 [docs/BENCHMARKS.md](../docs/BENCHMARKS.md) for methodology and results.
 
